# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.venv/
# .venv_baselines is separate on purpose: the baseline extractors pin lxml and
# nltk versions that conflict with the validated render path.
.venv_*/

# Benchmark corpora — the default landing site for `htmlsift acquire`, ~1.9 GB
# across the three boards. Read from here, never committed.
vendors/*/data/

# Top-level scratch: routing experiments, exported bundles, run logs, smoke
# outputs. CLAUDE.md §2 — data/ is ignored in full.
/data/

# results/ is committed, not ignored: it holds the rendered result tables
# (tools/download_results.py) that the writeup and README cite. Raw artifacts
# (weights, ledgers, caches) are covered by the extension/dir rules below.

# Weights, exports and embedding caches. Expensive to reproduce and not git's
# problem — they live on disk. Listed by extension as well as by directory
# because a stray copy outside the expected folder is the case that bites:
# GitHub hard-rejects any single file over 100 MB and git itself warns about
# nothing.
*.pt
*.pt.*
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.npy
*.npz
checkpoints/
cache/
embeddings/

# Corpora and per-record score dumps anywhere in the tree.
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.gz
*.tar.gz
# Test fixtures are the one carve-out. They must stay small enough to read.
!tests/**/fixtures/**

# Secrets
.env

# Tooling state — no project content
.claude/

# Local agent guidance, kept on disk but not published. AGENTS.md is the public
# overview; CLAUDE.md holds the local working notes and stays out of the repo.
CLAUDE.md

# Campaign scratch — the archive keeps these, this public repo does not
# (CLAUDE.md §10: no campaign journal, plan, or status file here).
/wmb_issues/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db